      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T11:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Could you double check if you\u0027re suggesting to `phandle` or `token`?\n\nSorry, I misclicked!\n\n\u003e Plus, what about `android,avf` instead? `pvmfw` seems pVM specific.\n\n`pvmfw` is the only one that will verify the token but you\u0027re right that the guest (for whatever reason) might want to also read it. Taking your comment one step further, there\u0027s nothing `avf` or even `android`-specific about this pKVM-defined token. Therefore, the name of the property should be defined by Linux, which won\u0027t be set in stone until the pvIOMMU driver gets upstreamed ... I guess, for now, `android,avf` makes sense as what we come up with here isn\u0027t guaranteed to be approved by upstream and we\u0027d have to support 2 bindings anyway.",
